{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-124146" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/assets/ac639fb08d54d2004aec96708ffd19bc080b028e739075687a84a09158cd4fd2.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x,$ where $C$ is the path along a semicircle of radius $2,$ traversed from the point $(2,1)$ to the point $(-2,1),$ shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/state.json" "file_sha256" "b17ac954cae06bb27e717726d39daf0dfb673322cc32aedb2cdbf4cacbf000d8"} {"question" "q-124146" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The line integral of unity with respect to $x$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $x$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x={x}_{2}-{x}_{1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{2}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the terminal point, and ${x}_{1}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, ${x}_{2}=-2$ and ${x}_{1}=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x={x}_{2}-{x}_{1}=(-2)-2=-4.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/state.json" "file_sha256" "b17ac954cae06bb27e717726d39daf0dfb673322cc32aedb2cdbf4cacbf000d8"} {"question" "q-124146" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8bc6f9dbda7d7db45fc648bd526ec9f400f366d03fe9b9c0445eed2bf9de20ad"} {"question" "q-124146" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-cap