rminal point, and ${y}_{1}$ is the $y$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, ${y}_{1}=4$ and  ${y}_{2}=-1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}y={y}_{2}-{y}_{1}=(-1)-4=-5.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/state.json" "file_sha256" "b17ac954cae06bb27e717726d39daf0dfb673322cc32aedb2cdbf4cacbf000d8"} {"question" "q-124342" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8bc6f9dbda7d7db45fc648bd526ec9f400f366d03fe9b9c0445eed2bf9de20ad"} {"question" "q-124342" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/state.json" "file_sha256" "b17ac954cae06bb27e717726d39daf0dfb673322cc32aedb2cdbf4cacbf000d8"} {"question" "q-124342" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-5"] ["math" "-9"] ["math" "2\\pi +3"] ["math" "4\\pi +5"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/state.json" "file_sha256" "b17ac954cae06bb27e717726d39daf0dfb673322cc32aedb2cdbf4cacbf000d8"} {"question" "q-124342" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/state.json" "file_sha256" "b17ac954cae06bb27e717726d39daf0dfb673322cc32aedb2cdbf4cacbf000d8"} {"question" "q-124148" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/assets/2400f92070b4f7d4e0ad0309574b729da86754bc64b6d7a3c508433d1bbc7f76.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}y,$ where $C$ is the path along the line segment between the points $(4,0)$ to the point $(0,3),$ as shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/state.json" "file_sha256" "b17ac954cae06bb27e717726d39daf0dfb673322cc32aedb2cdbf4cacbf000d8"} {"question" "q-124148" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The line integral of unity with respect to $y$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $y$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}y={y}_{2}-{y}_{1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{2}$ is the $y$-coordinate of the terminal point, and ${y}_{1}$ is the $y$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, ${y}_{2}=3$ and ${y}_{1}=0.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}y={y}_{2}-{y}_{1}=3-0=3.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/state.json" "file_sha256" "b17ac954cae06bb27e717726d39daf0dfb673322cc32aedb2cdbf4cacbf000d8"} {"question" "q-124148" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8bc6f9dbda7d7db45fc648bd526ec9f400f366d03fe9b9c0445eed2bf9de20ad"} {"question" "q-124148" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/state.json" "file_sha256" "b17ac954cae06bb27e717726d39daf0dfb673322cc32aedb2cdbf4cacbf000d8"} {"question" "q-124148" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4"] ["math" "-5"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/state.json" "file_sha256" "b17ac954cae06bb27e717726d39daf0dfb673322cc32aedb2cdbf4cacbf000d8"} {"question" "q-124148" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/state.json" "file_sha256" "b17ac954cae06bb27e717726d39daf0dfb673322cc32aedb2cdbf4cacbf000d8"} {"question" "q-124149" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=4$ and ${\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=6,$ calculate ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$ given that $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/state.json" "file_sha256" "b17ac954cae06bb27e717726d39daf0dfb673322cc32aedb2cdbf4cacbf000d8"} {"question" "q-124149" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $x,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4-6 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/state.json" "file_sha256" "b17ac954cae06bb27e717726d39daf0dfb673322cc32aedb2cdbf4cacbf000d8"} {"question" "q-124149" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8bc6f9dbda7d7db45fc648bd526ec9f400f366d03fe9b9c0445eed2bf9de20ad"} {"question" "q-124149" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/state.json" "file_sha256" "b17ac954cae06bb27e717726d39daf0dfb673322cc32aedb2cdbf4cacbf000d8"} {"question" "q-124149" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "10"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "24"] ["text" "Impossible to determine"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/state.json" "file_sha256" "b17ac954cae06bb27e717726d39daf0dfb673322cc32aedb2cdbf4cacbf000d8"} {"question" "q-124149" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/state.json" "file_sha256" "b17ac954cae06bb27e717726d39daf0dfb673322cc32aedb2cdbf4cacbf000d8"} {"question" "q-124179" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=3$ and ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=5,$ calculate ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$ given that $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/state.json" "file_sha256" "b17ac954cae06bb27e717726d39daf0dfb673322cc32aedb2cdbf4cacbf000d8"} {"question" "q-124179" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $y,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=-{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-3+5 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/state.json" "file_sha256" "b17ac954cae06bb27e717726d39daf0dfb673322cc32aedb2cdbf4cacbf000d8"} {"question" "q-124179" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8bc6f9dbda7d7db45fc648bd526ec9f400f366d03fe9b9c0445eed2bf9de20ad"} {"question" "q-124179" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/state.json" "file_sha256" "b17ac954cae06bb27e717726d39daf0dfb673322cc32aedb2cdbf4cacbf000d8"} {"question" "q-124179" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "7"] ["math" "8"] ["text" "Impossible to determine"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/state.json" "file_sha256" "b17ac954cae06bb27e717726d39daf0dfb673322cc32aedb2cdbf4cacbf000d8"} {"question" "q-124179" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/state.json" "file_sha256" "b17ac954cae06bb27e717726d39daf0dfb673322cc32aedb2cdbf4cacbf000d8"} {"question" "q-124182" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=14$ and ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=10,$ calculate ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$ given that $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/state.json" "file_sha256" "b17ac954cae06bb27e717726d39daf0dfb673322cc32aedb2cdbf4cacbf000d8"} {"question" "q-124182" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $x,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-14+10 \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/state.json" "file_sha256" "b17ac954cae06bb27e717726d39daf0dfb673322cc32aedb2cdbf4cacbf000d8"} {"question" "q-124182" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8bc6f9dbda7d7db45fc648bd526ec9f400f366d03fe9b9c0445eed2bf9de20ad"} {"question" "q-124182" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/state.json" "file_sha256" "b17ac954cae06bb27e717726d39daf0dfb673322cc32aedb2cdbf4cacbf000d8"} {"question" "q-124182" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-24"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "24"] ["math" "4"] ["text" "Impossible to determine"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/state.json" "file_sha256" "b17ac954cae06bb27e717726d39daf0dfb673322cc32aedb2cdbf4cacbf000d8"} {"question" "q-124182" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/state.json" "file_sha256" "b17ac954cae06bb27e717726d39daf0dfb673322cc32aedb2cdbf4cacbf000d8"} {"question" "q-124184" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=15$ and ${\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=10,$ calculate ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$ given that $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/state.json" "file_sha256" "b17ac954cae06bb27e717726d39daf0dfb673322cc32aedb2cdbf4cacbf000d8"} {"question" "q-124184" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $x,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$\n\nIn our case, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 15 & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 15 & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x-10 \\\\ 25 & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=-25.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/state.json" "file_sha256" "b17ac954cae06bb27e717726d39daf0dfb673322cc32aedb2cdbf4cacbf000d8"} {"question" "q-124184" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8bc6f9dbda7d7db45fc648bd526ec9f400f366d03fe9b9c0445eed2bf9de20ad"} {"question" "q-124184" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/state.json" "file_sha256" "b17ac954cae06bb27e717726d39daf0dfb673322cc32aedb2cdbf4cacbf000d8"} {"question" "q-124184" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-25"] ["math" "-5"] ["math" "20"] ["math" "25"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/state.json" "file_sha256" "b17ac954cae06bb27e717726d39daf0dfb673322cc32aedb2cdbf4cacbf000d8"} {"question" "q-124184" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-25"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/state.json" "file_sha256" "b17ac954cae06bb27e717726d39daf0dfb673322cc32aedb2cdbf4cacbf000d8"} {"question" "q-124188" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=21,$ ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=2,$ and ${\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=-11,$ calculate ${\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$ given that $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}\\cup {C}_{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/state.json" "file_sha256" "b17ac954cae06bb27e717726d39daf0dfb673322cc32aedb2cdbf4cacbf000d8"} {"question" "q-124188" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}\\cup {C}_{3}$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $x,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$\n\nIn our case, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -{\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & =2-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -21 & =2-(-11)+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -21 & =13+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -34 & ={\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=-34.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/state.json" "file_sha256" "b17ac954cae06bb27e717726d39daf0dfb673322cc32aedb2cdbf4cacbf000d8"} {"question" "q-124188" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8bc6f9dbda7d7db45fc648bd526ec9f400f366d03fe9b9c0445eed2bf9de20ad"} {"question" "q-124188" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/state.json" "file_sha256" "b17ac954cae06bb27e717726d39daf0dfb673322cc32aedb2cdbf4cacbf000d8"} {"question" "q-124188" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-12"] ["math" "-34"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "30"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/state.json" "file_sha256" "b17ac954cae06bb27e717726d39daf0dfb673322cc32aedb2cdbf4cacbf000d8"} {"question" "q-124188" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-34"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/state.json" "file_sha256" "b17ac954cae06bb27e717726d39daf0dfb673322cc32aedb2cdbf4cacbf000d8"} {"question" "e-9525" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int_C \\,\\textrm d x,$ where $C=C_1 \\cup C_2$ is the path comprising of two line segments, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/assets/3d408de0d50e2688aa0b35d8af39b6847cfdf21d5ec583320f0204384304fbc8.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/example-9525.json" "file_sha256" "566cb5dc511a46936fef50c4ba8809987216dd5c35e858ef9b0e2d054ddbce87"} {"question" "e-9525" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The line integral of unity with respect to $x$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $x$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\textrm d x = x_2 - x_1,\n$$\n\nwhere $x_2$ is the $x$-coordinate of the terminal point, and $x_1$ is the $x$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, $x_2 = -3$ and $x_1 = 3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\textrm d x = x_2 - x_1 = (-3) - 3 = -6.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/example-9525.json" "file_sha256" "566cb5dc511a46936fef50c4ba8809987216dd5c35e858ef9b0e2d054ddbce87"} {"question" "e-9526" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int_C \\,\\textrm d y,$ where $C$ is the path along the semicircle of radius $3,$ traversed from the point $(3,0)$ to the point $(-3,0),$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/assets/ca97546ecaf9e37bee53fcc2b0c66962cff67a91ee9b117cc8ac8531efa23efc.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/example-9526.json" "file_sha256" "8b5f345a0d9cb40b271588b99f7acf89cd02a1f8ccbd8c94097d114e3c8d581f"} {"question" "e-9526" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The line integral of unity with respect to $y$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $y$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\textrm d y = y_2 - y_1,\n$$\n\nwhere $y_2$ is the $y$-coordinate of the terminal point, and $y_1$ is the $y$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, $y_2 = 0$ and $y_1 = 0.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\textrm d y = y_2 - y_1 =  0 - 0 = 0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/example-9526.json" "file_sha256" "8b5f345a0d9cb40b271588b99f7acf89cd02a1f8ccbd8c94097d114e3c8d581f"} {"question" "e-9527" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $\\displaystyle\\int_{C} f(x,y) \\,\\textrm d x= 8$ and $\\displaystyle\\int_{-C_1} f(x,y) \\,\\textrm d x= -2,$ calculate $\\displaystyle\\int_{-C_2} f(x,y) \\,\\textrm d x$ given that $C = C_1\\cup C_2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/example-9527.json" "file_sha256" "94f7be52c3066f11f957d3c2c8901f0b7dadbfccab94d89e12702864509b14a4"} {"question" "e-9527" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $C = C_1\\cup C_2$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $x,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- $\\displaystyle\\int_{-C} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x = -\\int_{C} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x$\n\n- $\\displaystyle\\int_{C} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x = \\int_{C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x + \\int_{C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x$\n\nIn our case, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 8 & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 8 & =-(-2)-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 8 & =2-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 6 & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\int_{-C_2} f(x,y) \\,\\textrm d x = -6.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059897/example-9527.json" "file_sha256" "94f7be52c3066f11f957d3c2c8901f0b7dadbfccab94d89e12702864509b14a4"}] "usage" {"e-9527" [] "q-124147" [] "q-124149" [] "e-9525" [] "e-9526" [] "q-124148" [] "q-124146" []} "basis" 1909 "retractions" [[17592186179930 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3708/Source/Images/q-124146.png)\n\nCalculate $∫_{C}dx$, where $C$ is the path along a semicircle of radius $2$, traversed from the point $(2, 1)$ to the point $(-2, 1)$, shown above."] [17592186179931 :question/problem "Calculate $∮_{C}dx$, where $C$ is the closed path along the unit circle, traversed once in the counterclockwise direction."] [17592186179932 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3708/Source/Images/q-124148.png)\n\nCalculate $∫_{C}dy$, where $C$ is the path along the line segment between the points $(4, 0)$ to the point $(0, 3)$, as shown above."] [17592186179933 :question/problem "If $∫_{C_{1}}f(x, y)dx = 4$ and $∫_{-C_{2}}f(x, y)dx = 6$, calculate $∫_{C}f(x, y)dx$ given that $C = C_{1}∪C_{2}$."] [17592186179523 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int_C \\,\\textrm d x$, where $C=C_1 \\cup C_2$ is the path comprising of two line segments, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3708/Source/Images/8e812447b89c4e3aa73cf9f3313ab5fc.png)"] [17592186179523 :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to $x$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $x$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\textrm d x = x_2 - x_1\n$$\n\nwhere $x_2$ is the $x$-coordinate of the terminal point, and $x_1$ is the $x$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, $x_2 = -3$ and $x_1 = 3$. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\textrm d x = x_2 - x_1 = (-3) - 3 = -6\n$$"] [17592186179524 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int_C \\,\\textrm d y$, where $C$ is the path along the semicircle of radius $3$, traversed from the point $(3,0)$ to the point $(-3,0)$, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3708/Source/Images/57e461e49aa9411e4aeb899975abcd92.png)"] [17592186179524 :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to $y$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $y$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\textrm d y = y_2 - y_1\n$$\n\nwhere $y_2$ is the $y$-coordinate of the terminal point, and $y_1$ is the $y$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, $y_2 = 0$ and $y_1 = 0$. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\textrm d y = y_2 - y_1 = 0 - 0 = 0\n$$"] [17592186179525 :question/problem "If $\\displaystyle\\int_{C} f(x,y) \\,\\textrm d x= 8$ and $\\displaystyle\\int_{-C_1} f(x,y) \\,\\textrm d x= -2$, calculate $\\displaystyle\\int_{-C_2} f(x,y) \\,\\textrm d x$ given that $C = C_1\\cup C_2$."] [17592186179525 :question/worked-solution "Let\n\n$$\nC = C_1\\cup C_2\n$$\n\nbe a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation.\n\nFor line integrals with respect to $x$, we have the following properties:\n\n- $\\displaystyle\\int_{-C} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x = -\\int_{C} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x$\n- $\\displaystyle\\int_{C} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x = \\int_{C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x + \\int_{C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x$\n\nIn our case, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{C}f(x, y)dx &= ∫_{C_{1}}f(x, y)dx + ∫_{C_{2}}f(x, y)dx \\\\\n8 &= - ∫_{-C_{1}}f(x, y)dx - ∫_{-C_{2}}f(x, y)dx \\\\\n8 &= - (-2) - ∫_{-C_{2}}f(x, y)dx \\\\\n8 &= 2 - ∫_{-C_{2}}f(x, y)dx \\\\\n6 &= - ∫_{-C_{2}}f(x, y)dx\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\int_{-C_2} f(x,y) \\,\\textrm d x = -6\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186177581 17592186177582 17592186177583 17592186177584 17592186177585 17592186177587 17592186177588 17592186177589 17592186177590 17592186177591 17592186177593 17592186177594 17592186177595 17592186177596 17592186177597 17592186177599 17592186177600 17592186177601 17592186177602 17592186177603] "immutable_fields" [[17592186177580 :answer-field/correct] [17592186177580 :answer-field/id] [17592186177580 :answer-field/key] [17592186177580 :answer-field/type] [17592186177586 :answer-field/correct] [17592186177586 :answer-field/id] [17592186177586 :answer-field/key] [17592186177586 :answer-field/type] [17592186177592 :answer-field/correct] [17592186177592 :answer-field/id] [17592186177592 :answer-field/key] [17592186177592 :answer-field/type] [17592186177598 :answer-field/correct] [17592186177598 :answer-field/id] [17592186177598 :answer-field/key] [17592186177598 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
